    "Opt-in storage is one XRT value pointer at the tail of each instance allocation. Derived types inherit state support.",
    "Get retains the same value identity, Set retains and replaces the slot, and Context trace reports each real state edge.",
    "Read access continues inside type destructors. Writes after logical destruction are rejected. The native fixture replaces a member of a busy XRT object and requests widget destruction from its drop callback.",
    "Direct C O0/O2 and language JIT/dynamic/static AOT exercise 1000 warm reads and twice as many assignments with pre-existing values and allocations forbidden. The C fixture also compares heap counters.",
    "The language fixtures check mutable object identity, per-instance separation, prior owner lifetime after teardown, and regression of all nine virtual callbacks. The graphical example uses separate per-widget colors."
